' node_diagram_sim.puml
'
' ROS Node Design Diagram for the wall follower in simulation, drawn to the
' unit's Task 5 standard: one ellipse per running node, one arrow per
' publish/subscribe connection, arrows labelled with what they carry.
'
' WallFollower         our right wall follower (turtlebot3_drive executable,
'                      class CWallFollowerNode)
' RosGzBridge          ros_gz_bridge parameter_bridge: carries the simulated
'                      robot's laser, odometry and joint data out of Gazebo
'                      and the velocity command into it
' ImageBridge          ros_gz_image image_bridge: carries the simulated
'                      camera image out of Gazebo
' RobotStatePublisher  turns wheel joint angles into the pose of every link
' RViz                 displays the laser scan, camera image and path driven
'
' Everything except WallFollower is started by turtlebot3_maze.launch.py.

@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 55

usecase "RosGzBridge" as Bridge
usecase "WallFollower" as Follower
usecase "ImageBridge" as Image
usecase "RobotStatePublisher" as StatePub
usecase "RViz" as Rviz

Bridge --> Follower : laser_scan
Follower --> Bridge : velocity_command

Bridge --> StatePub : wheel_joint_angles
Bridge --> Rviz : laser_scan
Bridge --> Rviz : robot_odometry
StatePub --> Rviz : robot_link_poses
Image --> Rviz : camera_image
@enduml
